{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-virtual-subword","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:virtual-subword","kind":"definition","title":"Virtual subword, entanglement across a cut, and connected parts","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-virtual-particles-exceptional-divisor","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-jones-markov-trace"],"cites":["references/jones1985"],"tags":["virtual-particles","entanglement","observable","class-function","conjugation","linking-number","borromean","braid-word","cumulant","mobius-inversion","connected-part","jones-polynomial"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.VirtualSubword.IsVirtual","text":"virtual-subword.md","leanSource":"virtual-subword.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:virtual-subword\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G</code> be a group, standing for the braid group <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B_n</code> or its image in the Hecke algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n(q)</code>, and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> be a ring of values. A function <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f \\colon G \\to R</code> is an <strong>observable</strong> if <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f(xy) = f(yx)</code> for all <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">x, y \\in G</code>. Words <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a, b</code> are <strong>conjugate</strong>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a \\approx b</code>, if <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b = y a y^{-1}</code> for some <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">y</code>, and <strong>equal in normal form</strong>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a \\equiv b</code>, if they reduce to the same Gröbner–Shirshov normal form.</p>\n<p>Fix a set <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{O}</code> of observables. A subword <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">x</code> placed between <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">v</code> is <strong>virtual</strong> for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{O}</code> if</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  f(u\\,x\\,v) = f(u\\,v) \\quad \\text{for every } f \\in \\mathcal{O}.</code></pre>\n<p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">w</code> be a word on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code> strands and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A \\subset \\{1, \\dots, n\\}</code>. Write <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_A(w)</code> for the signed number of crossings between a strand in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> and a strand outside <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s_A(w)</code> for the signed number of the remaining crossings. The word is <strong>entangled across</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A \\mid A^{c}</code> if <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_A(w) \\neq 0</code>. A <strong>prior entangled pair</strong> is a pure subword that is entangled across the cut separating its two partners.</p>\n<p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F</code> assign a value in a commutative ring to each finite set <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code> of strands. Its <strong>connected part</strong> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code> is the Möbius inversion over subsets,</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\phi_F(T) = (-1)^{|T|} \\sum_{U \\subseteq T} (-1)^{|U|} F(U).</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.md","heading":"Definition","number":"17.20.9","page":"b/def-virtual-subword","lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.VirtualSubword.IsVirtual","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
